Expected elements: present

Presence verified with attention to the previously failing pair: the scrubber is present and shrunk, not hidden — a 160px track at x673–832 with its elapsed head filled — and the position readout `128 / 1315` is a separate element beside it, both legible. Provenance is the `DATA` row inside the Transaction pane, not a band. Code with the current line 32, the Call Trace | Event Log tab strip with Call Trace open and seven frames, Values with eleven values, both stepping directions in the bar.

Everything here is legible — the smallest text (`Field`, `DATA`, `FETCHING`, chip labels) sits at a 9px cap height and 7.3:1 or better, and the mono column in Values is genuinely scannable. The problem for a rubric that rewards density is how little the page carries for 1440×900.

It shows 26 code lines at a 23px pitch for 10px glyphs, 7 frames, 11 values and 8 metadata rows. Against that: 241px of blank in the tabbed region (49% of it), 142px of stacked header chrome in the Code pane before line 1 (17%), and 310px — 37% of the Transaction pane — spent on the eleven-line provenance paragraph. Roughly a third of the pixels are carrying nothing while seven code lines fade out at the right edge and the Transaction pane runs flush into its bottom border.

Fixes: tighten the code pitch and hand the tabbed region's 241px to the panes that are clipping.

Rating: 6/10

